Realtek RTL8125/RTL8126/RTL8127 Driver for illumos
==================================================

Overview
--------

This directory contains an illumos GLDv3 network driver for modern
Realtek PCIe Ethernet controllers, including:

    RTL8125   (up to 2.5 Gigabit Ethernet)
    RTL8126   (up to 5 Gigabit Ethernet)
    RTL8127   (up to 10 Gigabit Ethernet)

The driver is intended for newer RTL8125-class devices and later.
Legacy RTL8169 / RTL8168 / RTL8111 generations are outside the primary support
scope.

Origin
------

This driver includes material derived from the FreeBSD re(4) driver and
related Realtek hardware definitions.

Large portions of the hardware register definitions, PHY programming
sequences, descriptor formats and compatibility logic were originally
developed in the FreeBSD project.

The illumos version has been substantially reworked for:

    - GLDv3 MAC framework integration
    - illumos DMA interfaces
    - illumos interrupt framework
    - MSI-X multiqueue operation
    - kstat statistics
    - FMA topology temperature sensor integration
    - illumos driver lifecycle and attach/detach model

Features
--------

Current driver capabilities include:

    - MSI-X and MSI interrupt support
    - Multiqueue RX/TX operation
    - RSS receive scaling
    - Checksum offload
    - Configurable advertised link speeds
    - Timer interrupt compatibility mode
    - Temperature monitoring on supported chips
    - RTL8125B / RTL8126 / RTL8127 support

Configuration
-------------

Driver tunables may be placed in:

    /kernel/drv/re.conf

Example:

    force_msi=0;
    timer_int_enable=0;
    timer_count=9728;

Notes
-----

PCIe ASPM policy should normally be controlled by system firmware.
If unexplained stalls or interrupt loss occur, disabling ASPM in BIOS/UEFI
may improve stability on some systems.

